Before and After Scenario Explanation

Before (Old Process)

In the previous version of the Excel macro, the program used a fixed last row to determine the number of records to be processed.

Characteristics:

The macro only processed data up to a predefined last row value in the code.

If additional rows were added beyond this set limit, the macro could not detect or process them.

The SAP login credentials (username and password) were handled in the backend or hardcoded in the macro.

Users had to manually update the last row in the code whenever more data was added.


Issues Encountered:

Some records were not processed because they were located beyond the fixed last row.

This resulted in missing data in SAP, particularly users that were not included during the upload or processing.

Required manual monitoring and code adjustments to avoid missing records.


Limitations:

High risk of missing SAP user data.

Manual maintenance was required when the dataset increased.

Less flexible credential management due to hardcoded login details.



---

After (Improved Process)

In the improved version, enhancements were implemented to make the macro more dynamic, reliable, and easier to maintain.

Improvements:

1. Dynamic Last Row Detection

The macro now automatically identifies the last row with data in the worksheet.

This ensures that all available records are processed, regardless of how many rows are added.



2. Sheet-Based SAP Login Credentials

The SAP username and password are now stored in the Excel sheet.

The macro reads these values directly from the worksheet during execution.




Benefits:

Eliminates the issue of missing SAP user data caused by fixed row limitations.

Automatically processes all newly added records.

Reduces the need for manual code updates.

Makes the system more flexible and easier to maintain.



---

Summary of Improvements

Feature	Before	After

Last Row Handling	Fixed last row in code	Dynamic last row detection
Data Processing	Limited rows only	Processes all rows with data
SAP User Processing	Some users missing due to row limit	All users processed
SAP Credentials	Hardcoded / backend	Stored in Excel sheet
Maintenance	Requires manual code edits	Easily configurable



